    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. The original EvoSuite test has opaque variable names and magic numbers. Let me write a clearer version.\n\nKey observations:\n- `(byte) 49` is ASCII '1', so index 0 of the input represents the MSB '1'\n- The 8-byte array encodes the binary string \"10000000\" (MSB first)\n- `(byte)(-128)` is `0x80` — the decoded result of \"10000000\"The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces opaque EvoSuite-generated names (`binaryCodec0`, `byteArray0`, `byteArray1`) with meaningful ones (`codec`, `asciiInput`, `decoded`), uses `(byte) '1'` instead of the magic number `49`, uses `(byte) 0x80` instead of `(byte)(-128)`, and adds a comment explaining the bit-ordering logic so the expected output is no longer a mystery."
    }
